─── app/templates/pipeline_detail.html:14-14 ───
[bug · medium] Cancelled scene runs break the trailing retry-script. `cancel_run` can move a
`SCENE_SLICE` run from `SCENE_SLICE_QUEUE` to `CANCELLED` (pipeline_type stays `SCENE_SLICE`), and
the new scene action branch renders no `.retry-form` for that state — but the script at the bottom
(gated only on `run.pipeline_type != 'NVIDIA_CHUNK' and run.status in
['FAILED','QUARANTINED','CANCELLED']`) unconditionally does
`retryForm.querySelector('#retry-from')`, which throws an uncaught TypeError on the cancelled scene
detail page. Before this change the generic retry form was rendered for that state, so this
interaction is newly introduced. Guard the script (`if (retryForm) { ... }`) or add `and not
is_scene` to its condition.



─── app/templates/pipeline_detail.html:48-48 ───
[maintainability · medium] No code path writes `model_endpoint` or `model_identity` into a scene
run's `pipeline_config_snapshot_json` (the snapshot is built in `create_scene_run` with
schema_version/purpose/scenes/effective_config_hash/... and later touched only by
`record_scene_outcome`/`retry_run`), so this line will always render the "—（未登记）" fallback. If a
registration path is planned in a follow-up, confirm it; otherwise consider displaying what the
snapshot actually freezes (e.g. the per-scene `capability_config_hash` entries or the model profile
reference), since that is the real "远端模型服务身份" data available today.



─── app/templates/pipeline_detail.html:81-81 ───
[maintainability · low] The web layer (`app/web/pipelines.py`) already computes and passes
`scene_terminal` (SCENE_DONE / SCENE_FAILED / SCENE_PARTIAL_FAILED / CANCELLED / QUARANTINED /
INPUT_INVALID), but the template never uses it and hardcodes the scene terminal statuses here
instead. Two sources of truth will drift (e.g. `INPUT_INVALID` is in `scene_terminal` but not here).
Prefer using the server-computed variable (or dropping the unused one).



